# Summary
Introduced a production-reachable crash/failpoint in non-test code. It should be gated behind a test-only/process-test feature, debug-only configuration, or parsed as an explicit opt-in value unavailable in normal deployments.
The new process-level crash injection is not limited to tests or debug builds. `ControlPlaneRaftWalFile::append_record_for_log_store` now calls `maybe_exit_after_control_plane_raft_wal_file_sync()` after syncing the WAL file and its parent directory. That helper checks for `ARGMIN_EXPERIMENTAL_RAFT_EXIT_AFTER_PEER_WAL_BEFORE_RESPONSE` and unconditionally calls `std::process::exit(1)` if the variable exists, regardless of its value. This means a production binary launched with that environment variable, even set to `0` or an empty string, will terminate on Raft WAL appends. This is primarily a reliability/operational crash hazard rather than a remotely exploitable security vulnerability because the attacker would need control over the service environment or an operator would need to deploy with the hidden failpoint enabled.

# Resolution
Fixed in commit [dc7944fdc8df53850bd407780f0de78ace2c85b6](https://github.com/justincormack/argmin/commit/dc7944fdc8df53850bd407780f0de78ace2c85b6) (`Remove raft WAL process failpoint`).

The production-reachable WAL-sync exit hook and its environment-variable trigger were removed from `crates/storage/src/control_plane_raft.rs`, and the peer RPC worker no longer arms any WAL crash guard. The process coverage was rewritten to use normal production behavior: the test makes the restarted follower's state directory unwritable, sends a direct peer append, verifies checkpoint-before-response fails, and then proves the unacknowledged append is recoverable through the ordinary artifact-plus-WAL path. No feature gate or production failpoint remains.

# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Identify the failpoint environment variable and confirm it is not test/debug-gated in the changed storage code.
- [x] Confirm the public WAL append path reaches the failpoint after file and parent-directory sync.
- [x] Build a debug target with symbols and verify a baseline WAL append succeeds without the environment variable.
